  "brief": "<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Market Overview</h2>\n\nFutures are flat to slightly lower as Iran-US tensions continue to dominate headlines after three months of escalating conflict. S&P 500 at $750.33 (-0.02%) holding relatively steady while Russell 2000 showing weakness at $288.42 (-0.67%). VIX at 24.95 suggests elevated but not extreme fear levels.\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> What to Watch</h2>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Core PCE Data (12:30 ET)</strong> - Fed's preferred inflation gauge could drive rate expectations</li>\n<li><strong>Fed Jefferson Speech</strong> - Any commentary on current geopolitical risks and monetary policy</li>\n<li><strong>Building Permits (12:30 ET)</strong> - Housing data amid rising uncertainty</li>\n<li><strong>Continuing Jobless Claims</strong> - Labor market resilience check</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-red\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚠ Bear Case</div>Iran-US air strikes escalating with Kuwait now reporting missile intercepts. Energy supply disruption risk increasing as conflict spreads beyond initial scope.</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Sector Rotation</h2>\n\nHealth (+0.99%) and Energy (+0.67%) leading as defensive positioning intensifies around geopolitical risk. Industrials (-1.10%) and Materials (-0.98%) getting hammered on growth concerns. Tech holding up surprisingly well at +0.17% despite broader risk-off sentiment.\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-amber\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚡ Key Driver</div>Strait of Hormuz tensions are the primary market driver. Any escalation could spike energy prices further while any ceasefire talks could trigger risk-on rotation.</div>\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-green\"><div class=\"callout-label\">✦ Bull Case</div>VIX at 24.95 suggests fear is elevated but not panic levels. Markets have had three months to price in Iran risks, potential for relief rally if tensions de-escalate.</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Levels That Matter</h2>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>S&P 500:</strong> Support at $745, resistance at $755 - range-bound until geopolitical clarity</li>\n<li><strong>VIX:</strong> Watch for break above 27 (panic mode) or below 22 (risk-on return)</li>\n<li><strong>Energy (XLE):</strong> Breaking above recent highs on supply concerns</li>\n<li><strong>Russell 2000:</strong> Testing support at $285 - small caps vulnerable to uncertainty</li>\n</ul>\n\n<hr>\n<p><em>Not a prediction. A preparation. Make your plan before the bell.</em></p>"
